SCVHS (Specify, Construct, Validate, Harden, Ship) is a proprietary methodology
developed by NIIT Limited ("NIIT"). This repository contains the methodology
specification, terminology, templates, examples, and research documentation
that constitute the SCVHS methodology.

PERMITTED USES:
- NIIT employees and authorized contractors may use this methodology for
  instructional design, curriculum development, and delivery within NIIT programs.
- Learners enrolled in NIIT programs may use the templates and examples provided
  in this repository for their coursework.
- The research paper (docs/research-paper.md) may be cited in academic and
  professional contexts with full attribution to NIIT Limited.

PROHIBITED USES WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM NIIT LIMITED:
- Commercial use of the methodology or any part thereof
- Reproduction or distribution of the methodology specification, templates,
  or worked examples outside NIIT programs
- Creation of derivative works based on the SCVHS methodology
- Use of the SCVHS name, acronym, or proprietary terms (Comprehension Primitive,
  Decision Log as defined in SCVHS, Scaffolding Fade as defined in SCVHS,
  Ship-Backward Design) in any commercial or educational product
- Training or fine-tuning AI models on the content of this repository

INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY:
The following are proprietary to NIIT Limited:
- The SCVHS name and acronym as applied to the five-phase engineering methodology
- The Comprehension Primitive concept and specification
- The Decision Log concept, structure, and specification as defined in this repository
- The three-mode structure (Hand-First + Validate AI / Hybrid / Full SCVHS) and
  their definitions
- The Scaffolding Fade model as applied to AI construction modes
- Ship-Backward Design as a curriculum design methodology

